  "answer": "There is a stronger positive operator. For the normalized finite-volume BT law exp(-S)dpsi on the mean-zero carrier, the one-form Witten operator L1=L0 tensor I+Hess S obeys L1*d=d*L0 and has quadratic form ||d_mu_star v||^2+||dv||^2. It is nonnegative even where Hess S is indefinite. Hence the old pointwise orthogonal-Hessian and new low-action flat-Hessian witnesses do not obstruct this route. Splitting spatial one-forms into the lowest Fourier sector and its complement replaces the invalid pointwise Schur complement by the operator Schur complement of L1. A volume-uniform lower bound for that operator, or a controlled low-Rayleigh sequence, is now the precise undecided gate. No such bound is claimed here.",
